WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.400
Speaker 1: So we have another new headline&nbsp;
about the spending bill slash infrastructure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:11.840
bill discussion that continues to I don't want to&nbsp;
be negative, but it sort of is like plaguing us&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:17.360
at this point. The fact that this discussion and&nbsp;
grandstanding and people getting attention for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.000
getting getting attention, for opposing&nbsp;
things that they should be in favor of.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:31.040
But maybe this is good news and the news is that&nbsp;
House Democrats have put paid family leave back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:36.400
into the spending bill. Now I'm going to tell&nbsp;
you what the news is, and I'm going to tell you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:43.200
what's being said. But my view on this is that&nbsp;
this in and of itself may be grandstanding,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:48.080
and I don't know if I'm at this point, just&nbsp;
jaded and cynical. You'll have to tell me,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:53.280
but we'll get to that. Remember, the context is&nbsp;
that even as things were completely falling apart,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:59.280
Bernie Sanders went on TV over the weekend and&nbsp;
said, Hey, I'm still working on the prescription&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:05.600
drug cost control aspect of this. And then on&nbsp;
Tuesday, it was announced, Hey, the prescription&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:10.960
drug control component is back in the bill.&nbsp;
We talked about that a couple of days ago.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:16.400
Now the news is House Democrats put paid family&nbsp;
leave back into the bill. The Hill reporting House&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:21.200
Democrats have amended the enormous social&nbsp;
spending framework at the heart of President&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:26.720
Biden's economic agenda to include paid family&nbsp;
leave, a popular provision that had met resistance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:31.360
from Senator Joe Manchin and was thought to&nbsp;
be removed. The change was announced Wednesday&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:35.280
morning in a letter from Speaker Pelosi, who said&nbsp;
the House Rules Committee would meet later in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:40.400
day to consider the changes. But Pelosi stopped&nbsp;
short of announcing the vote on the package.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:44.160
Instead, the speaker said there&nbsp;
remain a few outstanding issues.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:49.280
It has been my intention through the process to&nbsp;
put on the House floor and pass a bill that would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:55.840
pass the Senate in the same form because I've been&nbsp;
informed by a senator of opposition to a few of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:59.600
the priorities contained in our bill, and because&nbsp;
we must have legislation agreed to by the House&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:03.920
and Senate in the final version of Build Back&nbsp;
Better that will we will send to the president's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:08.800
desk. We must strive to find common ground. Biden&nbsp;
initially proposed 12 weeks of paid family leave,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:16.000
a provision adopted by House Democrats, but&nbsp;
Manchin balked at the 490 $4 billion price tag,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:21.120
forcing negotiators to consider a sharp reduction&nbsp;
down to four weeks before Biden slashed it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:27.120
altogether. Progressives grumbled and said they&nbsp;
would accept that they would accept it as a cost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:32.400
of enacting other social benefits. Pelosi on&nbsp;
Wednesday, however, said paid leave would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:37.600
part of the House Rules Committee discussion.&nbsp;
The decision came at the urging of many members&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:42.320
of the cost conscious caucus. Chairman Richie&nbsp;
Neal and the committee staff have worked on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:48.880
this priority for a long time and were ready. The&nbsp;
provision will provide for weeks not the 12 four&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:54.720
weeks of permanent parental and medical leave,&nbsp;
according to an aide familiar with the language.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.760 --> 00:03:01.840
Alex Bolton reporting mansion, not thrilled to&nbsp;
hear Speaker Pelosi has added four weeks of paid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:08.960
leave back in BBB. That's a challenge and they&nbsp;
know how I feel about it. So, OK, first of all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:16.480
this isn't the infrastructure bill. This is the&nbsp;
2022 budget bill labeled Build Back Better or BBB.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:22.160
There's confusion between the two. Without a&nbsp;
doubt. Often it's not really. They just say&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:28.400
the bill. So there's confusion, but this is the&nbsp;
build back better bill. Now, in an ideal world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:34.160
everything would be in its own bill. So you say,&nbsp;
OK, let's do a bill for paid family leave. Who's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:39.520
for it? Who's against it? OK, you figure it&nbsp;
out. The problem is that if you did that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:44.800
a whole bunch of stuff would just never pass.&nbsp;
The whole system we have is this pseudo corrupt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:53.920
system of cronyism and earmarks and pork where&nbsp;
people in the House and Senate agree to support X&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.920 --> 00:04:00.720
as long as Y is in there. And that's sort of like&nbsp;
a for better or for worse thing. That's why we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:07.600
get these packages with so many things in there.&nbsp;
Now there are real questions as to how these four&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:12.480
weeks would even work. Do you have to pay into&nbsp;
it or not? What counts is leave. What's a worker?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:16.800
What about gig workers? What about self-employed&nbsp;
people, independent contractors? Does it only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:21.760
apply to W-2? We just don't know. And what's&nbsp;
the future of this? We have absolutely no idea.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:26.080
What I know is two things, and this is where&nbsp;
I want to go back to. Am I being too cynical?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:31.280
Time is running out to get this done this calendar&nbsp;
year to get this done before the House and Senate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:37.760
recess for the end of the year. I am starting to&nbsp;
wonder whether things are getting added back in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:46.000
so that it looks better as a bill that's&nbsp;
not going to pass. What I mean by that is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:52.720
one perspective is that build back better is&nbsp;
that the build back better act, at least in 2021,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:59.360
is not going to pass. So thinking very&nbsp;
cynically, are they making the bill more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:06.080
robust so that when it doesn't pass, they can&nbsp;
say, Look, we, we put our best foot forward.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:13.440
We added prescription drug controls. We added&nbsp;
some paid leave so that the bill looks better to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:19.840
progressives knowing that the bill is essentially&nbsp;
dead. They will not pass a better bill.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:27.200
Rather than not pass a crappier bill.&nbsp;
I don't know. It's all disappointing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:31.600
This has been going on for months at this&nbsp;
point. These are all things that should&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:36.160
not be controversial in a country as rich as the&nbsp;
United States. These things aren't controversial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:40.320
in most other countries that are level of wealth.&nbsp;
But don't me know if you think I'm being too&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:45.440
cynical about now, they're just trying to make&nbsp;
the bill better before not passing it to say&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:50.080
it would have been a pretty good bill, but it has&nbsp;
no chance of passing. Let me know what you think.

